---
title: FOSSBilling File Structure
description: Find the PHP application, frontend assets, modules, and themes in the FOSSBilling source tree.
---

The PHP application lives in `src/`, and shared frontend code and tooling live in `frontend/` at the repository root. A release installation uses the contents of `src/` at its root.

## Source Code

| Path | Purpose |
| ---- | ------- |
| `src/library/FOSSBilling/` | Core PHP classes, including API dispatch in `Api/` and the Twig environment in `Twig/`. |
| `src/library/Box/`, `src/library/Model/` | Application classes and legacy database models. |
| `src/library/Payment/Adapter/` | [Payment gateway adapters](/extensions-and-development/guides/creating-a-payment-gateway/). |
| `src/library/Registrar/Adapter/` | [Domain registrar adapters](/extensions-and-development/guides/creating-a-registrar-integration/). |
| `src/library/Server/Manager/` | [Server managers](/extensions-and-development/guides/creating-a-server-manager/) for hosting control panels. |
| `src/install/` | Browser-based installation wizard. |
| `src/data/` | Default location for cache files, logs, and uploads. See [file and folder permissions](/maintenance/troubleshooting/#file-and-folder-permissions). |
| `src/locale/` | Language files. See the [build guide](/getting-started/building/#build-steps) for adding translations to a source checkout. |
| `src/public/` | Shared public assets, including generated browser bundles, branding, and payment gateway icons. |
| `frontend/` | Shared browser code and build tooling. The [JavaScript API wrapper](/extensions-and-development/javascript/) builds from `frontend/core/api.ts` to `src/public/assets/js/api.js`. |

### `/src/modules`

A typical module includes its API, controllers, templates, and metadata.

{% filetree %}
- ModuleName/
  - Api/
    - Admin.php       # Admin API endpoints
    - Client.php      # Client API endpoints
    - Guest.php       # Guest/public API endpoints
  - Controller/
    - Admin.php       # Admin routes/controllers
    - Client.php      # Client routes/controllers
    - Guest.php       # Guest routes/controllers
  - templates/          # Module templates
    - admin/          # Admin panel templates
    - client/         # Client area templates
    - email/          # Email templates
  - manifest.json       # Module metadata
  - icon.svg            # Optional module icon (or icon.png, icon.webp, icon.avif; at most one)
  - Service.php         # Business logic
{% /filetree %}

[Guide: Creating a Module](/extensions-and-development/guides/creating-a-module/)

### `/src/themes`

Themes contain Twig templates, assets, and user overrides. See [Theme Structure](/extensions-and-development/guides/creating-a-theme/#theme-structure) for the directory layout.
